Map {
  "0.0.0" => "Hordes of monsters began laying siege to the kingdom of
Hyrule.",
  "0.1.0" => "Princess Zelda led a valiant defense against hopeless
odds.",
  "0.2.0" => "News of the Hyrulean army's imminent defeat reached the
cadets at the knights' training yard.",
  "0.4.0" => "As the elite troops fell in battle, Hyrule's trainees
were left to wait helplessly inside the castle walls.",
  "0.6.0" => "Despite the odds, one young knight took up his simple
training sword and chose to fight.",
  "0.7.0" => "This brave young man was named Link.",
  "0.8.0" => "Compelled to act, he rushed to the monster-ridden
battlefield to assist Zelda and defend Hyrule.",
  "0.10.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "0.11.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "0.12.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "0.13.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "0.14.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "1.0.0" => "After an arduous battle, Link and his comrades slew
King Dodongo, but the beast was only ever intended
as a distraction.",
  "1.1.0" => "The army of monsters had taken Hyrule Castle.",
  "1.3.0" => "Worse, after the dust had settled, Princess Zelda was
nowhere to be found.",
  "1.4.0" => "Impa and Link searched the battlefield for any sign of
her, but to no avail.",
  "1.5.0" => "Although the battle had been lost, Impa foresaw Link's
importance to the coming war.",
  "1.6.0" => "She bestowed upon him a green tunic--the sign of the
legendary hero.",
  "1.7.0" => "Link did not believe himself worthy of the honor, but he
was determined to help Impa and her remaining soldiers
locate Zelda.",
  "1.8.0" => "Weeks passed.",
  "1.9.0" => "Impa heard a rumor that a handful of soldiers were
holding out against the monsters in Faron Woods.",
  "1.10.0" => "The leader of this resistance was supposedly a young
woman.",
  "1.11.0" => "Impa dared to hope this unknown woman was Zelda.",
  "1.12.0" => "Link and Impa decided to make their way to the forest by
way of the Eldin Caves, a path with its own dangers.",
  "1.14.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "1.15.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "1.16.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "1.17.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "1.18.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "2.0.0" => "Link and his allies were saved from the dangers of the
Eldin Caves by a mysterious youth named Sheik.",
  "2.1.0" => "Joined by their new ally, Impa's troops exited the caves
and emerged in Faron Woods.",
  "2.2.0" => "There they found a hidden village overrun with monsters.",
  "2.3.0" => "While Link and Impa wanted to continue their search for
Zelda, they could not ignore the plight of the villagers.
Without hesitation, they sprang into battle.",
  "2.4.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "2.5.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "2.6.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "2.7.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "2.8.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "3.0.0" => "The leader of the resistance in Faron Woods was a
young sorceress named Lana.",
  "3.1.0" => "She was of the same clan as Cia, who had summoned
the monsters to Hyrule.",
  "3.2.0" => "Lana had been fighting Cia's army since it arrived.",
  "3.3.0" => "Cia now sought to complete the Triforce and use it to
conquer Hyrule.",
  "3.4.0" => "Link and Impa decided to join forces with Lana to
prevent further tragedy.",
  "3.5.0" => "Although the monsters of Faron Woods had been
defeated, Cia still controlled most of Hyrule.",
  "3.6.0" => "Every day more creatures appeared and swarmed the
land.",
  "3.7.0" => "Link and Impa fought on against the darkness, sorely
missing Zelda's leadership.",
  "3.8.0" => "Only one solution remained--stem the tide of monsters
by closing the Gate of Souls.",
  "3.9.0" => "The heroes headed to the Valley of Seers to put an end
to the bloodshed.",
  "3.10.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "3.11.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "3.12.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "3.13.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "3.14.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "4.0.0" => "Cia had already claimed the Triforce of Power.",
  "4.1.0" => "From Link she stole the Triforce of Courage.",
  "4.2.0" => "The Triforce of Wisdom was the birthright of the royal
family of Hyrule...",
  "4.3.0" => "yet Sheik bore it when Cia attacked.",
  "4.4.0" => "Once Cia possessed all the pieces of the Triforce...",
  "4.5.0" => "she used its incredible power to bend time and space
and open doorways through the ages.",
  "4.6.0" => "Portals to three eras appeared...",
  "4.7.0" => "Lana explained to the others that a Gate of Souls had
been opened in each of these eras, and it was through
these gates that the monsters came.",
  "4.8.0" => "By opening these gates, Cia had released the fragment
of evil's spirit imprisoned in each of the other eras.",
  "4.9.0" => "The task before the heroes was therefore to travel
through each portal and close its gate.",
  "4.10.0" => "Once all the gates were closed, they could begin
repairing the damage Cia had inflicted on their land.",
  "4.11.0" => "With time growing short, Link and his allies split up to
handle all three gates simultaneously.",
  "4.12.0" => "They each vowed to close their gate and return safely.",
  "4.13.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "4.14.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "4.15.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "4.16.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "4.17.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "5.0.0" => "Leading a small force of Hyrulean soldiers, Impa stepped
into one of the newly opened portals.",
  "5.1.0" => "The kingdom spread out before her seemed like the
Hyrule she knew, yet it was somehow very different.",
  "5.2.0" => "Before long, she realized that they had traveled
back to the era of the mythical Hero of Time.",
  "5.3.0" => "Awed, Impa began her search for the Gate of Souls.",
  "5.4.0" => "She sensed an evil presence on Death Mountain and
set out for the ominous peak.",
  "5.5.0" => "And with her came the mysterious Sheik...",
  "5.6.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "5.7.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "5.8.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "5.9.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "5.10.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "6.0.0" => "At the fairy's request, Impa had fought her way to the
summit of Death Mountain to rescue Princess Ruto.",
  "6.1.0" => "There she subdued the Goron chieftain, Darunia, who
had temporarily lost his senses.",
  "6.2.0" => "Upon freeing Princess Ruto, however, Impa was shocked
to learn the reason for the conflict between the Zora and
Goron people.",
  "6.3.0" => "The ancient Water Temple was teeming with monsters
that poured from the Gate of Souls.",
  "6.4.0" => "What's more, the monsters were apparently led by
Princess Zelda herself!",
  "6.5.0" => "Hoping to make sense of this disturbing revelation...",
  "6.6.0" => "Impa and her newfound allies journeyed to Lake Hylia.",
  "6.7.0" => "When they arrived, they were greeted by a Zelda
seemingly consumed by evil...",
  "6.8.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "6.9.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "6.10.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "6.11.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "6.12.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "7.0.0" => "Lana stepped through her portal and found a jarring
sight.",
  "7.1.0" => "Wherever she looked, the kingdom was consumed by
shadow.",
  "7.2.0" => "Though she knew of the Twilight Realm, she had
never seen it firsthand.",
  "7.3.0" => "Lana's sorcery could not reveal who or what was
causing the Twilight to cover Hyrule so completely.",
  "7.5.0" => "She soon came upon a small village beset by
monsters. Her mission to close the Gate of Souls
would have to wait...",
  "7.6.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "7.7.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "7.8.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "7.9.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "7.10.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "8.0.0" => "Lana had saved an unusual girl named Agitha from the
Twilight.",
  "8.1.0" => "To thank Lana for her rescue, Agitha gave her a
Goddess Butterfly, an insect that could guide her
wherever she wished to go.",
  "8.2.0" => "A curious Twili named Midna also joined the party for
reasons of her own.",
  "8.4.0" => "The heroes followed the Goddess Butterfly,
eventually arriving at the Palace of Twilight.",
  "8.5.0" => "There they met a terrible foe.",
  "8.6.0" => "It was Zant, the Usurper King of the Twilight Realm.",
  "8.7.0" => "Lana and Midna would have to overcome his unnatural
powers to complete their task.",
  "8.8.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "8.9.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "8.10.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "8.11.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "8.12.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "9.0.0" => "Link and his troops stepped through one of the portals,
appearing in an era of fantastical sights.",
  "9.1.0" => "He had heard tell of a land in the clouds, but now he
could see Skyloft with his own eyes...though he was not
the first new arrival.",
  "9.3.0" => "Overrun with monsters, the floating island faced imminent
destruction.",
  "9.4.0" => "Though vastly outnumbered, Link did not hesitate.",
  "9.5.0" => "He and his allies leapt into the fray to save Skyloft from
disaster.",
  "9.7.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "9.8.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "9.9.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "9.10.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "9.11.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "10.0.0" => "Fi, a servant of the goddess Hylia, joined Link, and
together they drove away the Dragon Knight Volga.",
  "10.1.0" => "But despite the victory, Ghirahim managed to slip away
in the chaos.",
  "10.3.0" => "Hoping to destroy Ghirahim and close the Gate of
Souls, Link followed Fi's advice and hurried to the
Sealed Grounds.",
  "10.4.0" => "The Hyrulean army advanced quickly in order to catch
up to their quarry.",
  "10.5.0" => "And that was when Ghirahim sprang his trap.",
  "10.6.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "10.7.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "10.8.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "10.9.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "10.10.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "11.0.0" => "With the Gate of Souls closed in each era, Link and his
allies were reunited.",
  "11.1.0" => "Sheik was at last revealed as Zelda, relieving much worry
about her fate.",
  "11.2.0" => "Meanwhile, Ganondorf had recovered three of his four
spirit fragments.",
  "11.3.0" => "He chose to leave Cia's body, her usefulness at an end.",
  "11.4.0" => "Free of Ganondorf's control but tragically corrupted,
Cia resolved to make Link and the Triforce hers and
hers alone.",
  "11.5.0" => "Using powerful rituals to strengthen her forces, she
redoubled her attacks on Hyrule.",
  "11.6.0" => "But all was not lost.",
  "11.7.0" => "Zelda directed her forces to the Temple of the Sacred
Sword in search of the one thing that could save
them all...",
  "11.8.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "11.9.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "11.10.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "11.11.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "11.12.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "12.0.0" => "At long last, Link took up the Master Sword and proved
himself the hero of legend.",
  "12.1.0" => "Armed as he was with the blade of evil's bane, Link
easily dispatched the newly revived Wizzro.",
  "12.2.0" => "The evil magician's parting words in their ears, Link and
his allies set out to confront Cia at the Temple of Souls.",
  "12.4.0" => "With a string of victories behind them, the Hyrulean
army's morale had improved remarkably.",
  "12.5.0" => "Even Link began to feel that he was invincible
while the Master Sword was in his hands.",
  "12.7.0" => "Soon he was allowing overconfidence to cloud his
judgment, rushing headlong into hordes of enemies.",
  "12.8.0" => "Cia had been waiting for Link to overextend himself,
giving her a chance to strike.",
  "12.9.0" => "And as the two sides battled, unknown eyes watched
from the shadows...",
  "12.10.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "12.11.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "12.12.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "12.13.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "12.14.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "13.0.0" => "Link's brashness nearly cost him his life as shadowy
doubles overwhelmed him.",
  "13.1.0" => "At the last moment, Link's allies salvaged a rescue from
otherwise certain defeat.",
  "13.2.0" => "The Master Sword is a mighty weapon...",
  "13.3.0" => "but its true power can be used only by someone who
understands the bonds of friendship.",
  "13.5.0" => "The Hyrulean army was rallying its strength, but Cia's
forces still controlled much of their homeland.",
  "13.6.0" => "The only way to save Hyrule was to defeat Cia.",
  "13.7.0" => "The Hyrulean army headed to the Valley of Seers to
force a decisive battle.",
  "13.8.0" => "But Cia did not sit idle, despite her overwhelming
advantage.",
  "13.9.0" => "She found new ways to fortify her troops using her
own life force. ",
  "13.10.0" => "The cost to herself was irrelevant, so long as she
crushed her enemies.",
  "13.11.0" => "The final battle between the armies of light and darkness
was about to unfold.",
  "13.12.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "13.13.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "13.14.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "13.15.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "13.16.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "14.0.0" => "Link and his friends defeated Cia and her legions,
returning peace to Hyrule.",
  "14.1.0" => "But that peace would be short lived.",
  "14.2.0" => "At the moment when Link drew the Master Sword from its
pedestal...",
  "14.3.0" => "he had inadvertently broken the seal on the last spirit
fragment's prison, setting it free to unite with the others.",
  "14.4.0" => "His spirit made whole, Ganondorf was reborn.",
  "14.5.0" => "His first act was to return to Gerudo Desert, the center
of his power in Hyrule.",
  "14.6.0" => "Once there, he summoned the spirits of Zant and Ghirahim
from their imprisonment to serve him.",
  "14.7.0" => "Finally, Ganondorf would hold the complete Triforce
in his hands and wield its full power.",
  "14.8.0" => "Knowing his enemies were approaching, he built a
stronghold in Gerudo Desert for the coming battles.",
  "14.9.0" => "With Zant and Ghirahim at his side, Ganondorf was
poised to conquer Hyrule.",
  "14.10.0" => "The future was bleak for the forces of light.",
  "14.11.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "14.12.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "14.13.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "14.14.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "14.15.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "15.0.0" => "With terrifying speed, the reborn Ganondorf raised his
army and fortified his position in Gerudo Desert.",
  "15.2.0" => "More powerful than ever, he moved to take the scattered
pieces of the Triforce.",
  "15.3.0" => "His first target was the Triforce of Power, still in Lana's
possession.",
  "15.5.0" => "Ganondorf had wielded it long ago and claimed it as
his right.",
  "15.7.0" => "Regaining it would give him the might to seize the other
two pieces.",
  "15.8.0" => "With this thought, Ganondorf led a massive army to
the Valley of Seers.",
  "15.9.0" => "Knowing she could never defeat him, Lana fled the valley
even as the Hyrulean army rushed to her aid.",
  "15.11.0" => "But Ganondorf outmaneuvered her and cut off her
retreat, attacking fiercely to retake the Triforce of
Power.",
  "15.12.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "15.13.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "15.14.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "15.15.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "15.16.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "16.0.0" => "Ganondorf's forces defeated the Hyrulean army and
wrenched the Triforce of Power from Lana's grasp.",
  "16.2.0" => "Yet, the other two pieces remained with Link and Zelda
in Hyrule Castle.",
  "16.3.0" => "If Ganondorf could take the castle and complete the
Triforce, Hyrule would be at his mercy.",
  "16.4.0" => "He readied his army for a siege.",
  "16.5.0" => "Meanwhile, Zelda's forces stood ready to defend their
home at all costs.",
  "16.6.0" => "Link stood at the head of the army, the shining
Triforce of Courage inspiring his troops.",
  "16.7.0" => "This battle would decide Hyrule's fate.",
  "16.8.0" => "Would the light endure...or would darkness spread to
every corner of the land?",
  "16.9.0" => "The next moments would decide.",
  "16.10.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "16.11.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "16.12.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "16.13.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "16.14.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "17.0.0" => "Ganondorf had assembled all three pieces of the
Triforce. With its unlimited might, he summoned
ever-greater hordes of monsters.",
  "17.1.0" => "Seeing that the battle was won, Ganondorf
vanished from sight.",
  "17.2.0" => "When Zelda learned of the Demon King's disappearance,
she saw a thin ray of hope.",
  "17.4.0" => "If the remaining Hyrulean army could defeat Zant and
Ghirahim in their master's absence, perhaps there was
a chance.",
  "17.5.0" => "Taking the fight to the enemy's stronghold in Gerudo
Desert, Zelda was determined to end the war before
the day was through.",
  "17.7.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "17.8.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "17.9.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "17.10.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "17.11.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "18.0.0" => "After Zelda's triumph in Gerudo Desert...",
  "18.1.0" => "Impa's forces managed to pinpoint Ganondorf's location.",
  "18.2.0" => "He had conquered Hyrule Castle and transformed it in
his own image. From this fortress, he prepared for an
unspeakable ritual.",
  "18.3.0" => "Link, Zelda, and all of their allies...",
  "18.4.0" => "from across the ages marched toward Ganon's Tower,
ready for the final, decisive battle.",
  "18.5.0" => "If they fell, all of Hyrule would fall with them...",
  "18.6.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "18.7.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "18.8.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "18.9.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "18.10.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "19.0.0" => "The goodness driven from her heart, Cia opened the
Gate of Souls, summoning vast hordes of monsters to
Hyrule.",
  "19.1.0" => "Ganondorf's spirit counseled that her attack must be
swift and devastating if she was to be victorious.",
  "19.2.0" => "However, controlling an army would require a
commander, and Cia realized she would need a
powerful warrior to serve as her general.",
  "19.3.0" => "The perfect candidate came readily to mind: the
Dragon Knight of the Eldin Caves.",
  "19.4.0" => "If he could be made to serve, such a creature would
easily be able to command her minions' obedience.",
  "19.5.0" => "Cia wasted no time.",
  "19.6.0" => "She immediately set off for the Eldin Caves in search
of her new champion.",
  "19.7.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "19.8.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "19.9.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "19.10.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "19.11.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "20.0.0" => "With Volga and Wizzro at the head of her army, Cia
launched her invasion of Hyrule.",
  "20.1.0" => "En route, Wizzro offered some advice.",
  "20.2.0" => "He said their first priority should be the eradication of
Hyrule's fairies.",
  "20.3.0" => "The good-hearted fairies of Hyrule were known to
provide aid and comfort to their chosen warriors.",
  "20.4.0" => "Should the legendary hero appear and receive their
assistance, Cia and her forces might be hard pressed.",
  "20.5.0" => "Cia considered Wizzro's counsel and commanded her
troops to begin hunting fairies.",
  "20.6.0" => "Many fairies were captured throughout Hyrule, but a
few eluded her grasp.",
  "20.7.0" => "Unbeknownst to Cia, a mysterious young woman was
working with the Gorons to protect the fairies.",
  "20.8.0" => "Rather than delay her invasion further, Cia dispatched
Volga and Wizzro to capture the last stragglers.",
  "20.9.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "20.10.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "20.11.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "20.12.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "20.13.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "21.0.0" => "Cia had conquered the land of Hyrule in the blink of
an eye and claimed pieces of the Triforce as the
spoils of her victory.",
  "21.1.0" => "Intoxicated by the power of the complete Triforce,
she fell further under Ganondorf's sway.",
  "21.2.0" => "At his urging, she ripped time and space open to
create portals to three other eras of Hyrule's storied
past.",
  "21.3.0" => "Immediately, she sensed a power emanating from the
Era of Twilight. She set off to discover whether it
was a resource to control...or an enemy to destroy.",
  "21.4.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "21.5.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "21.6.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "21.7.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "21.8.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "22.0.0" => "Cia sensed another powerful and unknown entity in a
separate rift in time, this one on the floating island of
Skyloft.",
  "22.1.0" => "When she arrived there, she found it already beset by
a vast army of monsters. But who commanded them,
Cia wondered.",
  "22.2.0" => "The inhabitants of Skyloft were clearly overwhelmed.
Many thought that the end of the world was at hand.",
  "22.3.0" => "Fi, a servant of the goddess, fought alongside the
humans, but the beasts' advance could not be
stopped.",
  "22.4.0" => "A great darkness would soon overtake Skyloft.
Though Cia cared nothing for the fate of the villagers,
she began formulating a plan.",
  "22.5.0" => "Whatever being had brought these creatures to Skyloft
would make a powerful servant. She would need to
subjugate it and make it her own.",
  "22.6.0" => "Launching herself into battle to defend Skyloft, Cia
looked for an opportunity to weaken this dark
power...and then add it to her forces.",
  "22.7.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "22.8.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "22.9.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "22.10.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "22.11.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "23.0.0" => "Link and his allies had defeated Wizzro, Zant, and
Ghirahim. Cia's hopes were fading.",
  "23.1.0" => "Meanwhile, Ganondorf was making his way to the
Valley of Seers to wrest the Triforce of Power from
her hands.",
  "23.2.0" => "Cia had few options remaining.",
  "23.3.0" => "Desperate to win at any cost, she tapped into her
very life force to bolster her magic.",
  "23.4.0" => "Cia knew this would cost her her life, but victory was
now worth any price.",
  "23.5.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "23.6.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "23.7.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "23.8.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "23.9.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "24.0.0" => "There once was a girl who lived in a small
village. She led a simple life, tending to her
flock of cuccos. Her name was Linkle.",
  "24.1.0" => "For as long as she could remember, Linkle had
believed in her heart that she was the hero reborn.",
  "24.2.0" => "One day, terrible news arrived at her village.",
  "24.3.0" => "Monsters had laid siege to Hyrule Castle.",
  "24.4.0" => "Linkle caught word of the monsters' attack
and immediately began preparations. She dressed
the part in her green tunic.",
  "24.5.0" => "Equipped with her trusty crossbows and the
ancient compass her grandmother had bestowed
on her, Linkle set out from the village.",
  "24.6.0" => "This treasured compass and a crude map were
all she had to guide her way to Hyrule Castle. ",
  "24.7.0" => "In no time at all, she found herself lost in a
malevolent forest.",
  "24.8.0" => "An imp in a curious mask appeared out of
nowhere and stole Linkle's precious compass.",
  "24.9.0" => "That compass, she knew, was proof of her
destiny. She had to get it back!",
  "24.10.0" => "And thus began Linkle's first true trial.",
  "24.11.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "24.12.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "24.13.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "24.14.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "24.15.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "25.0.0" => "At the Water Temple, Princess Zelda and Impa
had defeated Wizzro, the twisted wizard. They
returned to their own realm ahead of the others.",
  "25.1.0" => "Ruto and Darunia stayed behind in order to
patrol the grounds and keep vigil.",
  "25.2.0" => "But they suddenly found themselves drawn into
battle when they were attacked by a new wave of
monsters.",
  "25.3.0" => "It was the Dragon Knight, Volga, who led them.",
  "25.4.0" => "He set his wrath upon Ruto and Darunia,
and drew them into a vicious battle.",
  "25.5.0" => "It was then that Linkle, in her quest to find
Hyrule Castle, stumbled onto the scene.",
  "25.6.0" => "She was quick to answer Ruto's plea for aid, for
she knew a hero must always help those in need.
Linkle leapt into battle.",
  "25.7.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "25.8.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "25.9.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "25.10.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "25.11.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "26.0.0" => "The sorceress Cia had acquired the Triforce and
used it to bring forth other strange, new worlds.",
  "26.1.0" => "Not long after this, Ghirahim discovered a
Gate of Souls. It was in the Sealed Grounds
below Skyloft.",
  "26.2.0" => "Ghirahim knew a legendary beast was imprisoned
deep within the land. He gathered a horde of
monsters and plotted to awaken it.",
  "26.3.0" => "Far above, among the clouds of Skyloft,
the spirit Fi sensed disturbing changes
taking place in the land.",
  "26.4.0" => "Convinced that an evil force was stirring,
Fi quickly left Skyloft and flew down to the
Sealed Grounds.",
  "26.5.0" => "As Fi raced to the land below, an unexpected ally
stumbled upon the very same Sealed Grounds...",
  "26.6.0" => "It was Linkle. She had not yet found Hyrule Castle,
but she had managed to find another battle.",
  "26.7.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "26.8.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "26.9.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "26.10.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "26.11.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "27.0.0" => "Now that Link had acquired the Master Sword,
he and his companions began readying themselves
for the coming war with Cia.",
  "27.1.0" => "It was during this time that Princess Zelda
sensed an ominous presence.",
  "27.2.0" => "A dark magic, its source unknown, began to flow
across the land and devour everything it touched.",
  "27.3.0" => "If the flow of magic was not quickly stemmed,
all light would soon be gone from the world. ",
  "27.4.0" => "Believing the Palace of Twilight to be the
source of this devastation, Zelda set out on
her own to stop it.",
  "27.5.0" => "Midna soon noticed that the princess was gone.
She rushed after Zelda toward the palace.",
  "27.6.0" => "Along the way, Midna came upon Linkle,
who seemed to be utterly transfixed by
an object she had found.",
  "27.7.0" => "It was a black crystal, and Midna was mesmerized
by it as well. She touched the crystal.",
  "27.8.0" => "In the blink of an eye, Midna transformed
from a tiny creature into a beautiful woman.",
  "27.9.0" => "The powerful magic inside the crystal had returned
Midna to her true form.",
  "27.10.0" => "Linkle was left speechless, which was just
as well. There was no time to talk about
Midna's amazing transformation.",
  "27.11.0" => "Midna had only one thing on her mind: to rescue
Zelda. She recruited Linkle to join her mission.
Together, they would enter the Palace of Twilight.",
  "27.12.0" => "Her True Self",
  "27.13.0" => "Her True Self",
  "27.14.0" => "Her True Self",
  "27.15.0" => "Her True Self",
  "27.16.0" => "Her True Self",
  "28.0.0" => "The dark beast Ganon had been defeated by
Link and his allies. Hyrule Castle was free
from the clutches of the powerful darkness.",
  "28.1.0" => "Together, Zelda and Link set out for the
Temple of the Sacred Sword. There they would
seal away a fragment of the evil spirit.",
  "28.2.0" => "This, surely, would bring peace back to the land.",
  "28.3.0" => "Or so they believed. But no sooner had Link and
Zelda departed when a new horde of monsters
approached Hyrule Castle.",
  "28.4.0" => "Ganondorf had fallen, and the monsters were
left without a leader. But still, they showed
no hesitation in attacking innocent Hyruleans.",
  "28.5.0" => "Without Link or Zelda, or the allies who had
come to their aid from other worlds, Hyrule Castle
was left quite defenseless.",
  "28.6.0" => "In order to protect the people of the land,
Impa gathered together battle-weary soldiers
whose wounds had not even begun to heal.",
  "28.7.0" => "This, then, would be their sacrifice for Hyrule.
They fought as valiantly as they could.",
  "28.8.0" => "At that moment, a girl approached the battlefield.",
  "28.9.0" => "Linkle's journey had been plagued by false starts
from the moment she left her village. But she had
finally arrived at Hyrule Castle.",
  "28.10.0" => "She witnessed the brave soldiers struggling to
defeat the attacking monsters.",
  "28.11.0" => "Their courage kindled her spirit, and Linkle knew
that the time had come to fulfill her destiny.",
  "28.12.0" => "She gripped tightly the compass hanging around
her neck and readied herself to save Hyrule.",
  "28.13.0" => "Without another thought, Linkle leapt into the
fray amid the hordes of screeching monsters.",
  "28.14.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "28.15.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "28.16.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "28.17.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "28.18.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "29.0.0" => "Though peace was expected to return to Hyrule
after Ganon's fall, something rather ominous
happened instead.",
  "29.1.0" => "A new world appeared--a world of a different
dimension.",
  "29.2.0" => "Impa had summoned Link to Hyrule Castle.",
  "29.3.0" => "She asked him to investigate this strange
happening. Once the preparations for his
adventure were complete, Link set off.",
  "29.4.0" => "He entered this strange new world. It was
a vast, mysterious dimension with an unfamiliar
landscape.",
  "29.5.0" => "There he met a girl who was battling monsters.",
  "29.6.0" => "Her name was Tetra.",
  "29.7.0" => "She was the leader of a gang of pirates.
But she had become separated from her
crew during the recent dimensional event.",
  "29.8.0" => "Though strangers, the two could agree on
one thing: the monsters Tetra was battling
had to be defeated.",
  "29.9.0" => "They joined forces to take on the enemy.",
  "29.10.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "29.11.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "29.12.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "29.13.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "29.14.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "30.0.0" => "A short time before the strange happenings
washed over the Kingdom of Hyrule...",
  "30.1.0" => "Lana had returned to the Valley of Seers,
where she used sorcery to search for clues
to the vanished Cia.",
  "30.2.0" => "It was there that a figure appeared and stole
away the Triforce of Power.",
  "30.3.0" => "It took Lana by such surprise that she never
had a chance to identify the thieving villain. ",
  "30.4.0" => "At this point the strange happening in Hyrule
occurred, and Link was sent off to investigate.",
  "30.5.0" => "Lana sensed that a Gate of Souls had appeared
in Gerudo Desert.",
  "30.6.0" => "She also sensed that she might be able to
uncover new clues to Cia's disappearance,
if only she visited that spot.",
  "30.7.0" => "And so Lana left behind the Valley of Seers
and set off for Gerudo Desert.",
  "30.8.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "30.9.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "30.10.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "30.11.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "30.12.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "31.0.0" => "Link, Lana, and Tetra heeded the ancient king's
advice and headed for a place of great darkness.",
  "31.1.0" => "Tetra resolved to fight alongside Link and Lana
until this world had returned to normal.",
  "31.2.0" => "For she knew she could not sit idly by if someone
lurking in her own world was the reason behind
these strange happenings.",
  "31.3.0" => "Upon nearing their destination, the trio could
feel the power of the darkness grow stronger.",
  "31.4.0" => "As the darkness enveloped her, Lana began
to strongly sense Cia's presence in the land.",
  "31.5.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "31.6.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "31.7.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "31.8.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "31.9.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "32.0.0" => "The heroes now knew the evil one had taken
the Triforce of Power. He had robbed Cia of her
magic and learned of her other half, Lana.",
  "32.1.0" => "With the balance of the Triforce so shifted,
there was little hope the world would return
to normal.",
  "32.2.0" => "And with her magic gone, in time
Cia would completely disappear.",
  "32.3.0" => "Cia used what little power she had left to seek
out the one who had taken from her so much.
She told Link and the others of her findings.",
  "32.4.0" => "If they could defeat the shadowy presence,
they could save not only the world from
danger, but Cia as well.",
  "32.5.0" => "Link and his allies held the promise of future
peace in their hearts as they readied for this
final, decisive battle.",
  "32.6.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "32.7.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "32.8.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "32.9.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "32.10.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "34.0.0" => "Hordes of monsters began laying siege to the kingdom of
Hyrule.",
  "34.1.0" => "Princess Zelda led a valiant defense against hopeless
odds.",
  "34.2.0" => "News of the Hyrulean army's imminent defeat reached the
cadets at the knights' training yard.",
  "34.4.0" => "As the elite troops fell in battle, Hyrule's trainees
were left to wait helplessly inside the castle walls.",
  "34.6.0" => "Despite the odds, one young knight took up his simple
training sword and chose to fight.",
  "34.7.0" => "This brave young man was named Link.",
  "34.8.0" => "Compelled to act, he rushed to the monster-ridden
battlefield to assist Zelda and defend Hyrule.",
  "34.10.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "34.11.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "34.12.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "34.13.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "34.14.0" => "The Armies of Ruin",
  "35.0.0" => "After an arduous battle, Link and his comrades slew
King Dodongo, but the beast was only ever intended
as a distraction.",
  "35.1.0" => "The army of monsters had taken Hyrule Castle.",
  "35.3.0" => "Worse, after the dust had settled, Princess Zelda was
nowhere to be found.",
  "35.4.0" => "Impa and Link searched the battlefield for any sign of
her, but to no avail.",
  "35.5.0" => "Although the battle had been lost, Impa foresaw Link's
importance to the coming war.",
  "35.6.0" => "She bestowed upon him a green tunic--the sign of the
legendary hero.",
  "35.7.0" => "Link did not believe himself worthy of the honor, but he
was determined to help Impa and her remaining soldiers
locate Zelda.",
  "35.8.0" => "Weeks passed.",
  "35.9.0" => "Impa heard a rumor that a handful of soldiers were
holding out against the monsters in Faron Woods.",
  "35.10.0" => "The leader of this resistance was supposedly a young
woman.",
  "35.11.0" => "Impa dared to hope this unknown woman was Zelda.",
  "35.12.0" => "Link and Impa decided to make their way to the forest by
way of the Eldin Caves, a path with its own dangers.",
  "35.14.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "35.15.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "35.16.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "35.17.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "35.18.0" => "The Sheikah Tribesman",
  "36.0.0" => "Link and his allies were saved from the dangers of the
Eldin Caves by a mysterious youth named Sheik.",
  "36.1.0" => "Joined by their new ally, Impa's troops exited the caves
and emerged in Faron Woods.",
  "36.2.0" => "There they found a hidden village overrun with monsters.",
  "36.3.0" => "While Link and Impa wanted to continue their search for
Zelda, they could not ignore the plight of the villagers.
Without hesitation, they sprang into battle.",
  "36.4.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "36.5.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "36.6.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "36.7.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "36.8.0" => "The Sorceress of the Woods",
  "37.0.0" => "The leader of the resistance in Faron Woods was a
young sorceress named Lana.",
  "37.1.0" => "She was of the same clan as Cia, who had summoned
the monsters to Hyrule.",
  "37.2.0" => "Lana had been fighting Cia's army since it arrived.",
  "37.3.0" => "Cia now sought to complete the Triforce and use it to
conquer Hyrule.",
  "37.4.0" => "Link and Impa decided to join forces with Lana to
prevent further tragedy.",
  "37.5.0" => "Although the monsters of Faron Woods had been
defeated, Cia still controlled most of Hyrule.",
  "37.6.0" => "Every day more creatures appeared and swarmed the
land.",
  "37.7.0" => "Link and Impa fought on against the darkness, sorely
missing Zelda's leadership.",
  "37.8.0" => "Only one solution remained--stem the tide of monsters
by closing the Gate of Souls.",
  "37.9.0" => "The heroes headed to the Valley of Seers to put an end
to the bloodshed.",
  "37.10.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "37.11.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "37.12.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "37.13.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "37.14.0" => "The Sorceress of the Valley",
  "38.0.0" => "Cia had already claimed the Triforce of Power.",
  "38.1.0" => "From Link she stole the Triforce of Courage.",
  "38.2.0" => "The Triforce of Wisdom was the birthright of the royal
family of Hyrule...",
  "38.3.0" => "yet Sheik bore it when Cia attacked.",
  "38.4.0" => "Once Cia possessed all the pieces of the Triforce...",
  "38.5.0" => "she used its incredible power to bend time and space
and open doorways through the ages.",
  "38.6.0" => "Portals to three eras appeared...",
  "38.7.0" => "Lana explained to the others that a Gate of Souls had
been opened in each of these eras, and it was through
these gates that the monsters came.",
  "38.8.0" => "By opening these gates, Cia had released the fragment
of evil's spirit imprisoned in each of the other eras.",
  "38.9.0" => "The task before the heroes was therefore to travel
through each portal and close its gate.",
  "38.10.0" => "Once all the gates were closed, they could begin
repairing the damage Cia had inflicted on their land.",
  "38.11.0" => "With time growing short, Link and his allies split up to
handle all three gates simultaneously.",
  "38.12.0" => "They each vowed to close their gate and return safely.",
  "38.13.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "38.14.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "38.15.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "38.16.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "38.17.0" => "Separate Ways",
  "39.0.0" => "Leading a small force of Hyrulean soldiers, Impa stepped
into one of the newly opened portals.",
  "39.1.0" => "The kingdom spread out before her seemed like the
Hyrule she knew, yet it was somehow very different.",
  "39.2.0" => "Before long, she realized that they had traveled
back to the era of the mythical Hero of Time.",
  "39.3.0" => "Awed, Impa began her search for the Gate of Souls.",
  "39.4.0" => "She sensed an evil presence on Death Mountain and
set out for the ominous peak.",
  "39.5.0" => "And with her came the mysterious Sheik...",
  "39.6.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "39.7.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "39.8.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "39.9.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "39.10.0" => "Land of Myth",
  "40.0.0" => "At the fairy's request, Impa had fought her way to the
summit of Death Mountain to rescue Princess Ruto.",
  "40.1.0" => "There she subdued the Goron chieftain, Darunia, who
had temporarily lost his senses.",
  "40.2.0" => "Upon freeing Princess Ruto, however, Impa was shocked
to learn the reason for the conflict between the Zora and
Goron people.",
  "40.3.0" => "The ancient Water Temple was teeming with monsters
that poured from the Gate of Souls.",
  "40.4.0" => "What's more, the monsters were apparently led by
Princess Zelda herself!",
  "40.5.0" => "Hoping to make sense of this disturbing revelation...",
  "40.6.0" => "Impa and her newfound allies journeyed to Lake Hylia.",
  "40.7.0" => "When they arrived, they were greeted by a Zelda
seemingly consumed by evil...",
  "40.8.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "40.9.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "40.10.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "40.11.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "40.12.0" => "The Water Temple",
  "41.0.0" => "Lana stepped through her portal and found a jarring
sight.",
  "41.1.0" => "Wherever she looked, the kingdom was consumed by
shadow.",
  "41.2.0" => "Though she knew of the Twilight Realm, she had
never seen it firsthand.",
  "41.3.0" => "Lana's sorcery could not reveal who or what was
causing the Twilight to cover Hyrule so completely.",
  "41.5.0" => "She soon came upon a small village beset by
monsters. Her mission to close the Gate of Souls
would have to wait...",
  "41.6.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "41.7.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "41.8.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "41.9.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "41.10.0" => "Land of Twilight",
  "42.0.0" => "Lana had saved an unusual girl named Agitha from the
Twilight.",
  "42.1.0" => "To thank Lana for her rescue, Agitha gave her a
Goddess Butterfly, an insect that could guide her
wherever she wished to go.",
  "42.2.0" => "A curious Twili named Midna also joined the party for
reasons of her own.",
  "42.4.0" => "The heroes followed the Goddess Butterfly,
eventually arriving at the Palace of Twilight.",
  "42.5.0" => "There they met a terrible foe.",
  "42.6.0" => "It was Zant, the Usurper King of the Twilight Realm.",
  "42.7.0" => "Lana and Midna would have to overcome his unnatural
powers to complete their task.",
  "42.8.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "42.9.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "42.10.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "42.11.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "42.12.0" => "The Shadow King",
  "43.0.0" => "Link and his troops stepped through one of the portals,
appearing in an era of fantastical sights.",
  "43.1.0" => "He had heard tell of a land in the clouds, but now he
could see Skyloft with his own eyes...though he was not
the first new arrival.",
  "43.3.0" => "Overrun with monsters, the floating island faced imminent
destruction.",
  "43.4.0" => "Though vastly outnumbered, Link did not hesitate.",
  "43.5.0" => "He and his allies leapt into the fray to save Skyloft from
disaster.",
  "43.7.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "43.8.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "43.9.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "43.10.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "43.11.0" => "Land in the Sky",
  "44.0.0" => "Fi, a servant of the goddess Hylia, joined Link, and
together they drove away the Dragon Knight Volga.",
  "44.1.0" => "But despite the victory, Ghirahim managed to slip away
in the chaos.",
  "44.3.0" => "Hoping to destroy Ghirahim and close the Gate of
Souls, Link followed Fi's advice and hurried to the
Sealed Grounds.",
  "44.4.0" => "The Hyrulean army advanced quickly in order to catch
up to their quarry.",
  "44.5.0" => "And that was when Ghirahim sprang his trap.",
  "44.6.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "44.7.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "44.8.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "44.9.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "44.10.0" => "Sealed Ambition",
  "45.0.0" => "With the Gate of Souls closed in each era, Link and his
allies were reunited.",
  "45.1.0" => "Sheik was at last revealed as Zelda, relieving much worry
about her fate.",
  "45.2.0" => "Meanwhile, Ganondorf had recovered three of his four
spirit fragments.",
  "45.3.0" => "He chose to leave Cia's body, her usefulness at an end.",
  "45.4.0" => "Free of Ganondorf's control but tragically corrupted,
Cia resolved to make Link and the Triforce hers and
hers alone.",
  "45.5.0" => "Using powerful rituals to strengthen her forces, she
redoubled her attacks on Hyrule.",
  "45.6.0" => "But all was not lost.",
  "45.7.0" => "Zelda directed her forces to the Temple of the Sacred
Sword in search of the one thing that could save
them all...",
  "45.8.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "45.9.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "45.10.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "45.11.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "45.12.0" => "The Sacred Sword",
  "46.0.0" => "At long last, Link took up the Master Sword and proved
himself the hero of legend.",
  "46.1.0" => "Armed as he was with the blade of evil's bane, Link
easily dispatched the newly revived Wizzro.",
  "46.2.0" => "The evil magician's parting words in their ears, Link and
his allies set out to confront Cia at the Temple of Souls.",
  "46.4.0" => "With a string of victories behind them, the Hyrulean
army's morale had improved remarkably.",
  "46.5.0" => "Even Link began to feel that he was invincible
while the Master Sword was in his hands.",
  "46.7.0" => "Soon he was allowing overconfidence to cloud his
judgment, rushing headlong into hordes of enemies.",
  "46.8.0" => "Cia had been waiting for Link to overextend himself,
giving her a chance to strike.",
  "46.9.0" => "And as the two sides battled, unknown eyes watched
from the shadows...",
  "46.10.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "46.11.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "46.12.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "46.13.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "46.14.0" => "A War of Spirit",
  "47.0.0" => "Link's brashness nearly cost him his life as shadowy
doubles overwhelmed him.",
  "47.1.0" => "At the last moment, Link's allies salvaged a rescue from
otherwise certain defeat.",
  "47.2.0" => "The Master Sword is a mighty weapon...",
  "47.3.0" => "but its true power can be used only by someone who
understands the bonds of friendship.",
  "47.5.0" => "The Hyrulean army was rallying its strength, but Cia's
forces still controlled much of their homeland.",
  "47.6.0" => "The only way to save Hyrule was to defeat Cia.",
  "47.7.0" => "The Hyrulean army headed to the Valley of Seers to
force a decisive battle.",
  "47.8.0" => "But Cia did not sit idle, despite her overwhelming
advantage.",
  "47.9.0" => "She found new ways to fortify her troops using her
own life force. ",
  "47.10.0" => "The cost to herself was irrelevant, so long as she
crushed her enemies.",
  "47.11.0" => "The final battle between the armies of light and darkness
was about to unfold.",
  "47.12.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "47.13.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "47.14.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "47.15.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "47.16.0" => "Shining Beacon",
  "48.0.0" => "Link and his friends defeated Cia and her legions,
returning peace to Hyrule.",
  "48.1.0" => "But that peace would be short lived.",
  "48.2.0" => "At the moment when Link drew the Master Sword from its
pedestal...",
  "48.3.0" => "he had inadvertently broken the seal on the last spirit
fragment's prison, setting it free to unite with the others.",
  "48.4.0" => "His spirit made whole, Ganondorf was reborn.",
  "48.5.0" => "His first act was to return to Gerudo Desert, the center
of his power in Hyrule.",
  "48.6.0" => "Once there, he summoned the spirits of Zant and Ghirahim
from their imprisonment to serve him.",
  "48.7.0" => "Finally, Ganondorf would hold the complete Triforce
in his hands and wield its full power.",
  "48.8.0" => "Knowing his enemies were approaching, he built a
stronghold in Gerudo Desert for the coming battles.",
  "48.9.0" => "With Zant and Ghirahim at his side, Ganondorf was
poised to conquer Hyrule.",
  "48.10.0" => "The future was bleak for the forces of light.",
  "48.11.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "48.12.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "48.13.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "48.14.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "48.15.0" => "Ganondorf's Return",
  "49.0.0" => "With terrifying speed, the reborn Ganondorf raised his
army and fortified his position in Gerudo Desert.",
  "49.2.0" => "More powerful than ever, he moved to take the scattered
pieces of the Triforce.",
  "49.3.0" => "His first target was the Triforce of Power, still in Lana's
possession.",
  "49.5.0" => "Ganondorf had wielded it long ago and claimed it as
his right.",
  "49.7.0" => "Regaining it would give him the might to seize the other
two pieces.",
  "49.8.0" => "With this thought, Ganondorf led a massive army to
the Valley of Seers.",
  "49.9.0" => "Knowing she could never defeat him, Lana fled the valley
even as the Hyrulean army rushed to her aid.",
  "49.11.0" => "But Ganondorf outmaneuvered her and cut off her
retreat, attacking fiercely to retake the Triforce of
Power.",
  "49.12.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "49.13.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "49.14.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "49.15.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "49.16.0" => "March of the Demon King",
  "50.0.0" => "Ganondorf's forces defeated the Hyrulean army and
wrenched the Triforce of Power from Lana's grasp.",
  "50.2.0" => "Yet, the other two pieces remained with Link and Zelda
in Hyrule Castle.",
  "50.3.0" => "If Ganondorf could take the castle and complete the
Triforce, Hyrule would be at his mercy.",
  "50.4.0" => "He readied his army for a siege.",
  "50.5.0" => "Meanwhile, Zelda's forces stood ready to defend their
home at all costs.",
  "50.6.0" => "Link stood at the head of the army, the shining
Triforce of Courage inspiring his troops.",
  "50.7.0" => "This battle would decide Hyrule's fate.",
  "50.8.0" => "Would the light endure...or would darkness spread to
every corner of the land?",
  "50.9.0" => "The next moments would decide.",
  "50.10.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "50.11.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "50.12.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "50.13.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "50.14.0" => "Battle of the Triforce",
  "51.0.0" => "Ganondorf had assembled all three pieces of the
Triforce. With its unlimited might, he summoned
ever-greater hordes of monsters.",
  "51.1.0" => "Seeing that the battle was won, Ganondorf
vanished from sight.",
  "51.2.0" => "When Zelda learned of the Demon King's disappearance,
she saw a thin ray of hope.",
  "51.4.0" => "If the remaining Hyrulean army could defeat Zant and
Ghirahim in their master's absence, perhaps there was
a chance.",
  "51.5.0" => "Taking the fight to the enemy's stronghold in Gerudo
Desert, Zelda was determined to end the war before
the day was through.",
  "51.7.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "51.8.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "51.9.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "51.10.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "51.11.0" => "Enduring Resolve",
  "52.0.0" => "After Zelda's triumph in Gerudo Desert...",
  "52.1.0" => "Impa's forces managed to pinpoint Ganondorf's location.",
  "52.2.0" => "He had conquered Hyrule Castle and transformed it in
his own image. From this fortress, he prepared for an
unspeakable ritual.",
  "52.3.0" => "Link, Zelda, and all of their allies...",
  "52.4.0" => "from across the ages marched toward Ganon's Tower,
ready for the final, decisive battle.",
  "52.5.0" => "If they fell, all of Hyrule would fall with them...",
  "52.6.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "52.7.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "52.8.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "52.9.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "52.10.0" => "Liberation of the Triforce",
  "53.0.0" => "The goodness driven from her heart, Cia opened the
Gate of Souls, summoning vast hordes of monsters to
Hyrule.",
  "53.1.0" => "Ganondorf's spirit counseled that her attack must be
swift and devastating if she was to be victorious.",
  "53.2.0" => "However, controlling an army would require a
commander, and Cia realized she would need a
powerful warrior to serve as her general.",
  "53.3.0" => "The perfect candidate came readily to mind: the
Dragon Knight of the Eldin Caves.",
  "53.4.0" => "If he could be made to serve, such a creature would
easily be able to command her minions' obedience.",
  "53.5.0" => "Cia wasted no time.",
  "53.6.0" => "She immediately set off for the Eldin Caves in search
of her new champion.",
  "53.7.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "53.8.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "53.9.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "53.10.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "53.11.0" => "The Dragon of the Caves",
  "54.0.0" => "With Volga and Wizzro at the head of her army, Cia
launched her invasion of Hyrule.",
  "54.1.0" => "En route, Wizzro offered some advice.",
  "54.2.0" => "He said their first priority should be the eradication of
Hyrule's fairies.",
  "54.3.0" => "The good-hearted fairies of Hyrule were known to
provide aid and comfort to their chosen warriors.",
  "54.4.0" => "Should the legendary hero appear and receive their
assistance, Cia and her forces might be hard pressed.",
  "54.5.0" => "Cia considered Wizzro's counsel and commanded her
troops to begin hunting fairies.",
  "54.6.0" => "Many fairies were captured throughout Hyrule, but a
few eluded her grasp.",
  "54.7.0" => "Unbeknownst to Cia, a mysterious young woman was
working with the Gorons to protect the fairies.",
  "54.8.0" => "Rather than delay her invasion further, Cia dispatched
Volga and Wizzro to capture the last stragglers.",
  "54.9.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "54.10.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "54.11.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "54.12.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "54.13.0" => "The Invasion Begins",
  "55.0.0" => "Cia had conquered the land of Hyrule in the blink of
an eye and claimed pieces of the Triforce as the
spoils of her victory.",
  "55.1.0" => "Intoxicated by the power of the complete Triforce,
she fell further under Ganondorf's sway.",
  "55.2.0" => "At his urging, she ripped time and space open to
create portals to three other eras of Hyrule's storied
past.",
  "55.3.0" => "Immediately, she sensed a power emanating from the
Era of Twilight. She set off to discover whether it
was a resource to control...or an enemy to destroy.",
  "55.4.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "55.5.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "55.6.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "55.7.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "55.8.0" => "The Usurper King",
  "56.0.0" => "Cia sensed another powerful and unknown entity in a
separate rift in time, this one on the floating island of
Skyloft.",
  "56.1.0" => "When she arrived there, she found it already beset by
a vast army of monsters. But who commanded them,
Cia wondered.",
  "56.2.0" => "The inhabitants of Skyloft were clearly overwhelmed.
Many thought that the end of the world was at hand.",
  "56.3.0" => "Fi, a servant of the goddess, fought alongside the
humans, but the beasts' advance could not be
stopped.",
  "56.4.0" => "A great darkness would soon overtake Skyloft.
Though Cia cared nothing for the fate of the villagers,
she began formulating a plan.",
  "56.5.0" => "Whatever being had brought these creatures to Skyloft
would make a powerful servant. She would need to
subjugate it and make it her own.",
  "56.6.0" => "Launching herself into battle to defend Skyloft, Cia
looked for an opportunity to weaken this dark
power...and then add it to her forces.",
  "56.7.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "56.8.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "56.9.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "56.10.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "56.11.0" => "The Demon Lord",
  "57.0.0" => "Link and his allies had defeated Wizzro, Zant, and
Ghirahim. Cia's hopes were fading.",
  "57.1.0" => "Meanwhile, Ganondorf was making his way to the
Valley of Seers to wrest the Triforce of Power from
her hands.",
  "57.2.0" => "Cia had few options remaining.",
  "57.3.0" => "Desperate to win at any cost, she tapped into her
very life force to bolster her magic.",
  "57.4.0" => "Cia knew this would cost her her life, but victory was
now worth any price.",
  "57.5.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "57.6.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "57.7.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "57.8.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "57.9.0" => "Darkness Falls",
  "58.0.0" => "There once was a girl who lived in a small
village. She led a simple life, tending to her
flock of cuccos. Her name was Linkle.",
  "58.1.0" => "For as long as she could remember, Linkle had
believed in her heart that she was the hero reborn.",
  "58.2.0" => "One day, terrible news arrived at her village.",
  "58.3.0" => "Monsters had laid siege to Hyrule Castle.",
  "58.4.0" => "Linkle caught word of the monsters' attack
and immediately began preparations. She dressed
the part in her green tunic.",
  "58.5.0" => "Equipped with her trusty crossbows and the
ancient compass her grandmother had bestowed
on her, Linkle set out from the village.",
  "58.6.0" => "This treasured compass and a crude map were
all she had to guide her way to Hyrule Castle. ",
  "58.7.0" => "In no time at all, she found herself lost in a
malevolent forest.",
  "58.8.0" => "An imp in a curious mask appeared out of
nowhere and stole Linkle's precious compass.",
  "58.9.0" => "That compass, she knew, was proof of her
destiny. She had to get it back!",
  "58.10.0" => "And thus began Linkle's first true trial.",
  "58.11.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "58.12.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "58.13.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "58.14.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "58.15.0" => "The Girl in the Green Tunic",
  "59.0.0" => "At the Water Temple, Princess Zelda and Impa
had defeated Wizzro, the twisted wizard. They
returned to their own realm ahead of the others.",
  "59.1.0" => "Ruto and Darunia stayed behind in order to
patrol the grounds and keep vigil.",
  "59.2.0" => "But they suddenly found themselves drawn into
battle when they were attacked by a new wave of
monsters.",
  "59.3.0" => "It was the Dragon Knight, Volga, who led them.",
  "59.4.0" => "He set his wrath upon Ruto and Darunia,
and drew them into a vicious battle.",
  "59.5.0" => "It was then that Linkle, in her quest to find
Hyrule Castle, stumbled onto the scene.",
  "59.6.0" => "She was quick to answer Ruto's plea for aid, for
she knew a hero must always help those in need.
Linkle leapt into battle.",
  "59.7.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "59.8.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "59.9.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "59.10.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "59.11.0" => "Powers Collide",
  "60.0.0" => "The sorceress Cia had acquired the Triforce and
used it to bring forth other strange, new worlds.",
  "60.1.0" => "Not long after this, Ghirahim discovered a
Gate of Souls. It was in the Sealed Grounds
below Skyloft.",
  "60.2.0" => "Ghirahim knew a legendary beast was imprisoned
deep within the land. He gathered a horde of
monsters and plotted to awaken it.",
  "60.3.0" => "Far above, among the clouds of Skyloft,
the spirit Fi sensed disturbing changes
taking place in the land.",
  "60.4.0" => "Convinced that an evil force was stirring,
Fi quickly left Skyloft and flew down to the
Sealed Grounds.",
  "60.5.0" => "As Fi raced to the land below, an unexpected ally
stumbled upon the very same Sealed Grounds...",
  "60.6.0" => "It was Linkle. She had not yet found Hyrule Castle,
but she had managed to find another battle.",
  "60.7.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "60.8.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "60.9.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "60.10.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "60.11.0" => "The Demon Lord's Plan",
  "61.0.0" => "Now that Link had acquired the Master Sword,
he and his companions began readying themselves
for the coming war with Cia.",
  "61.1.0" => "It was during this time that Princess Zelda
sensed an ominous presence.",
  "61.2.0" => "A dark magic, its source unknown, began to flow
across the land and devour everything it touched.",
  "61.3.0" => "If the flow of magic was not quickly stemmed,
all light would soon be gone from the world. ",
  "61.4.0" => "Believing the Palace of Twilight to be the
source of this devastation, Zelda set out on
her own to stop it.",
  "61.5.0" => "Midna soon noticed that the princess was gone.
She rushed after Zelda toward the palace.",
  "61.6.0" => "Along the way, Midna came upon Linkle,
who seemed to be utterly transfixed by
an object she had found.",
  "61.7.0" => "It was a black crystal, and Midna was mesmerized
by it as well. She touched the crystal.",
  "61.8.0" => "In the blink of an eye, Midna transformed
from a tiny creature into a beautiful woman.",
  "61.9.0" => "The powerful magic inside the crystal had returned
Midna to her true form.",
  "61.10.0" => "Linkle was left speechless, which was just
as well. There was no time to talk about
Midna's amazing transformation.",
  "61.11.0" => "Midna had only one thing on her mind: to rescue
Zelda. She recruited Linkle to join her mission.
Together, they would enter the Palace of Twilight.",
  "61.12.0" => "Her True Self",
  "61.13.0" => "Her True Self",
  "61.14.0" => "Her True Self",
  "61.15.0" => "Her True Self",
  "61.16.0" => "Her True Self",
  "62.0.0" => "The dark beast Ganon had been defeated by
Link and his allies. Hyrule Castle was free
from the clutches of the powerful darkness.",
  "62.1.0" => "Together, Zelda and Link set out for the
Temple of the Sacred Sword. There they would
seal away a fragment of the evil spirit.",
  "62.2.0" => "This, surely, would bring peace back to the land.",
  "62.3.0" => "Or so they believed. But no sooner had Link and
Zelda departed when a new horde of monsters
approached Hyrule Castle.",
  "62.4.0" => "Ganondorf had fallen, and the monsters were
left without a leader. But still, they showed
no hesitation in attacking innocent Hyruleans.",
  "62.5.0" => "Without Link or Zelda, or the allies who had
come to their aid from other worlds, Hyrule Castle
was left quite defenseless.",
  "62.6.0" => "In order to protect the people of the land,
Impa gathered together battle-weary soldiers
whose wounds had not even begun to heal.",
  "62.7.0" => "This, then, would be their sacrifice for Hyrule.
They fought as valiantly as they could.",
  "62.8.0" => "At that moment, a girl approached the battlefield.",
  "62.9.0" => "Linkle's journey had been plagued by false starts
from the moment she left her village. But she had
finally arrived at Hyrule Castle.",
  "62.10.0" => "She witnessed the brave soldiers struggling to
defeat the attacking monsters.",
  "62.11.0" => "Their courage kindled her spirit, and Linkle knew
that the time had come to fulfill her destiny.",
  "62.12.0" => "She gripped tightly the compass hanging around
her neck and readied herself to save Hyrule.",
  "62.13.0" => "Without another thought, Linkle leapt into the
fray amid the hordes of screeching monsters.",
  "62.14.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "62.15.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "62.16.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "62.17.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "62.18.0" => "The Other Hero",
  "63.0.0" => "Though peace was expected to return to Hyrule
after Ganon's fall, something rather ominous
happened instead.",
  "63.1.0" => "A new world appeared--a world of a different
dimension.",
  "63.2.0" => "Impa had summoned Link to Hyrule Castle.",
  "63.3.0" => "She asked him to investigate this strange
happening. Once the preparations for his
adventure were complete, Link set off.",
  "63.4.0" => "He entered this strange new world. It was
a vast, mysterious dimension with an unfamiliar
landscape.",
  "63.5.0" => "There he met a girl who was battling monsters.",
  "63.6.0" => "Her name was Tetra.",
  "63.7.0" => "She was the leader of a gang of pirates.
But she had become separated from her
crew during the recent dimensional event.",
  "63.8.0" => "Though strangers, the two could agree on
one thing: the monsters Tetra was battling
had to be defeated.",
  "63.9.0" => "They joined forces to take on the enemy.",
  "63.10.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "63.11.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "63.12.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "63.13.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "63.14.0" => "A New Disturbance",
  "64.0.0" => "A short time before the strange happenings
washed over the Kingdom of Hyrule...",
  "64.1.0" => "Lana had returned to the Valley of Seers,
where she used sorcery to search for clues
to the vanished Cia.",
  "64.2.0" => "It was there that a figure appeared and stole
away the Triforce of Power.",
  "64.3.0" => "It took Lana by such surprise that she never
had a chance to identify the thieving villain. ",
  "64.4.0" => "At this point the strange happening in Hyrule
occurred, and Link was sent off to investigate.",
  "64.5.0" => "Lana sensed that a Gate of Souls had appeared
in Gerudo Desert.",
  "64.6.0" => "She also sensed that she might be able to
uncover new clues to Cia's disappearance,
if only she visited that spot.",
  "64.7.0" => "And so Lana left behind the Valley of Seers
and set off for Gerudo Desert.",
  "64.8.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "64.9.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "64.10.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "64.11.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "64.12.0" => "The Search for Cia",
  "65.0.0" => "Link, Lana, and Tetra heeded the ancient king's
advice and headed for a place of great darkness.",
  "65.1.0" => "Tetra resolved to fight alongside Link and Lana
until this world had returned to normal.",
  "65.2.0" => "For she knew she could not sit idly by if someone
lurking in her own world was the reason behind
these strange happenings.",
  "65.3.0" => "Upon nearing their destination, the trio could
feel the power of the darkness grow stronger.",
  "65.4.0" => "As the darkness enveloped her, Lana began
to strongly sense Cia's presence in the land.",
  "65.5.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "65.6.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "65.7.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "65.8.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "65.9.0" => "Reclaiming the Darkness",
  "66.0.0" => "The heroes now knew the evil one had taken
the Triforce of Power. He had robbed Cia of her
magic and learned of her other half, Lana.",
  "66.1.0" => "With the balance of the Triforce so shifted,
there was little hope the world would return
to normal.",
  "66.2.0" => "And with her magic gone, in time
Cia would completely disappear.",
  "66.3.0" => "Cia used what little power she had left to seek
out the one who had taken from her so much.
She told Link and the others of her findings.",
  "66.4.0" => "If they could defeat the shadowy presence,
they could save not only the world from
danger, but Cia as well.",
  "66.5.0" => "Link and his allies held the promise of future
peace in their hearts as they readied for this
final, decisive battle.",
  "66.6.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "66.7.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "66.8.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "66.9.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
  "66.10.0" => "Watchers of the Triforce",
}